data/sources/immigration-detention/doj-petition-26-104.txt-26-(1) In the Supreme Court of the United States No. XX-XX PHILIP L. RHONEY, ACTING FIELD OFFICE DIRECTOR, BUFFALO FIELD OFFICE, U.S. IMMIGRATION AND CUSTOMS ENFORCEMENT, PETITIONER v. RICARDO APARECIDO BARBOSA DA CUNHA ON PETITION FOR A WRIT OF CERTIORARI TO THE UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS FOR THE SECOND CIRCUIT PETITION FOR A WRIT OF CERTIORARI OPINIONS BELOW The opinion of the court of appeals (App., infra, 1a68a) is reported at 175 F.4th 61. The decision and order of the district court (App., infra, 69a-85a) is available at 2025 WL 3280575. JURISDICTION The judgment of the court of appeals was entered on April 28, 2026. The jurisdiction of this Court is invoked under 28 U.S.C. 1254(1). STATUTORY PROVISIONS INVOLVED The pertinent statutory provisions are reproduced in the appendix to this petition. App., infra, 86a-102a.
